bank-siglip2-base.npy, bank-siglip2-b32.npy, bank-siglip2-so400m.npy,
bank-pe-core-b16.npy

SigLIP 2 base (google/siglip2-base-patch16-224), B/32
(google/siglip2-base-patch32-256), So400m (google/siglip2-so400m-patch14-224,
through Immich's ONNX export) and Perception Encoder's PE core B/16 (Meta,
Apache 2.0, through onnx-community's ONNX export) text embeddings, rounded to
float16, of the same 4,096 descriptions from the training split of DiDeMo;
SigLIP 2 base's and PE core B/16's by their text towers with their weights in
8 bits, as whenframe searches with them since the twelfth round:

    Lisa Anne Hendricks, Oliver Wang, Eli Shechtman, Josef Sivic, Trevor Darrell
    and Bryan Russell. Localizing Moments in Video with Natural Language.
    ICCV 2017. https://github.com/LisaAnne/LocalizingMoments
    (released under the BSD 2-Clause license)

The descriptions were drawn at random (seed 0) among those of training videos
outside the benchmark's tuning set; `bank()` in scripts/didemo.py rebuilds
them from the annotations. The file holds embeddings only: no description
text and no video.

temporal-siglip2-base.npz, temporal-pe-core-b16.npz

whenframe's temporal models (whenframe/temporal.py), applied by default to the
frames of a new library (`whenframe index --no-temporal` leaves them out). temporal-siglip2-base.npz is model v3 of
docs/PROTOCOL.md's seventh round, on SigLIP 2 B/16's frames;
temporal-pe-core-b16.npz is model v4 of its ninth round, the same recipe on
PE core B/16's frames, which a library searches with v3's. Each is one
run of scripts/temporal.py on the frames and descriptions of

- DiDeMo's training videos: Flickr videos from YFCC100M, each under its own
  Creative Commons licence (some of them non-commercial), with descriptions
  released under the BSD 2-Clause license, and TEMPO-HL's sentences on them
  (Hendricks et al., EMNLP 2018, BSD 2-Clause license);
- MSR-VTT's training clips: YouTube clips with their descriptions (Xu et al.,
  CVPR 2016, Microsoft Research), published for research;
- Charades-STA's training videos: Charades (Sigurdsson et al., ECCV 2016),
  licensed for non-commercial research by the Allen Institute for AI, with
  Charades-STA's sentences (Gao et al., ICCV 2017);
- YouCook2's training videos: YouTube cooking videos with their steps (Zhou
  et al., AAAI 2018), published for research.

These videos were published for research. The weights are provided for
research and non-commercial use only; the rest of whenframe stays under the
MIT licence. The files hold weights only (v3's, also the speech settings and
sound weight chosen with it on the tuning sets, docs/PROTOCOL.md): no frame,
description or video.
